    <statement><p>For the region <m>R</m> below, write <m>\iint_R f\,dA</m>
as an iterated integral in polar coordinates.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap16Sec4__Q03__pg-image-1.png" width="41%"/>
<p>With
<m>a =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <m>b =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/>,
<m>c =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, and <m>d =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0004"/>,</p>
<p><m>\iint_R f\,dA = \int_a^b\!\!\int_c^d\, f\,dA</m>, where
<m>dA =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/> <m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0006"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0007"/></p>
<p><alert> Note:</alert> Use <m>t</m> for <m>\theta</m> in your expressions.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-\pi }{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
